From b95797a748e3823430905e81162f5e061924065c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 17:18:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] chat : drop whitespace between reasoning end tag and content

K2-Horizon (and any other tag-based reasoning model) can leave a plain
formatting newline right after its reasoning close tag, most visibly
when the reasoning block itself is empty at low effort. The generated
PEG parser had nothing consuming that gap: analyze_content::build_parser
went straight from the reasoning parser's closer into the content
capture, so the newline landed at the front of "content" instead of
being dropped like the whitespace already discarded from a
whitespace-only reasoning_content.

Reproduced live: 2/10 requests to K2-Horizon-7B (reasoning_effort low,
reasoning_format auto) returned content starting with "\n". The other
8/10 returned correct content, some prefixed with the model's own ": "
text, which must not be stripped.

Fix: consume optional whitespace with p.space() right after the
reasoning parser, before content starts -- the same pattern already
used for the JSON response-format path in build_parser. Applied to
both analyze_content::build_parser branches (always-wrapped and
stray-ends), gated on ctx.extracting_reasoning so a model with no
reasoning tags at all keeps any leading whitespace it genuinely emits.

Added test-chat.cpp cases: empty reasoning + newline, empty reasoning +
": " (must be preserved), non-empty reasoning + double newline. Live
recheck after the fix: 0/10 leading-whitespace content.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5
(cherry picked from commit 599dd43b0edefced31b94ace3e5cc34dce838077)
---
 common/chat-auto-parser-generator.cpp | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/common/chat-auto-parser-generator.cpp b/common/chat-auto-parser-generator.cpp
index b78789d8c0..f929546445 100644
--- a/common/chat-auto-parser-generator.cpp
+++ b/common/chat-auto-parser-generator.cpp
@@ -161,10 +161,18 @@ common_peg_parser analyze_content::build_parser(parser_build_context & ctx) cons
 
     if (is_always_wrapped()) {
         if (ctx.extracting_reasoning) {
-            return ctx.reasoning_parser + start + p.content(p.until(end)) + end + p.end();
+            // p.space() drops any whitespace the model leaves between the reasoning end tag
+            // and the content start tag (e.g. an empty K2-Horizon reasoning block followed by
+            // a formatting newline) so it never lands at the front of content.
+            return ctx.reasoning_parser + p.space() + start + p.content(p.until(end)) + end + p.end();
         }
         return p.content(p.until(start)) + start + p.content(p.until(end)) + end + p.end();
     }
+    if (ctx.extracting_reasoning) {
+        // Drop whitespace between the reasoning end tag and the content, only when reasoning was
+        // actually parsed out, so a model with no reasoning tags keeps any leading whitespace it emits.
+        return ctx.reasoning_parser + p.space() + p.content(p.rest()) + p.end();
+    }
     return ctx.reasoning_parser + p.content(p.rest()) + p.end();
 }
 
